    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/12/mizuno-hyperwarp-pure-review-2026.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The full-length PEBA setup (34 mm heel / 30.5 mm forefoot) is moderately soft-compliant with solid impact protection, but the feel is aggressive and forefoot-driven rather than plush.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is a standout, with a highly resilient, propulsive, and snappy toe-off from the stiff carbon-plated geometry, especially at faster paces.",
        "Stability: Torsional/overall rigidity is high (very stiff, not flexible), and lateral support is good from the wide platform and secure upper, but medial stability is limited and there is no formal heel counter.",
        "Durability: Outsole traction is strong on wet roads and tight turns, while overall outsole/material longevity is described as average rather than exceptional."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/12/mizuno-hyperwrap-pure-multi-tester.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is soft-but-firm with more ground feel due to the 34/30.5 mm stack and 3.5 mm drop; it feels less protective than higher-stack supershoes, with one tester saying it lacked enough protection for a marathon.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return and pop were standout traits, with strong propulsion from the PEBA foam plus full-length carbon plate; testers described it as quick, snappy, and eager to accelerate.",
        "Stability: It was considered reasonably stable for a supershoe, supported by the lower stack and moderately wide platform; heel lockdown/lateral hold were good, though the low drop initially challenged one tester’s stride/calves.",
        "Durability: The G3 outsole delivered strong grip and showed no visible wear after about 40 miles, indicating solid early material longevity; the main outsole issue reported was squeaky noise, not wear."
      ]
    }
  ],
